What failed:
`PointerHandle::leave` called `deactivate()` on the surface's constraint even when it was not
active, so the client got a second `unlocked` or `unconfined`: after an explicit deactivate, on
destruction, and for a persistent constraint that was never activated (W-SM-4c,
`docs/foundation/FOUNDATION_TEST_PLAN.md` OB-11).

Owner decision and date:
OB-11 Option B, adopted by the owner on 2026-10-07 under D-B12-PIN.

Upstream status:
Not sent: the issue is an outward action left to the owner (OB-11). Smithay `master` has the same
guard (`if constraint.is_active()` in `leave`, read 2026-11-26); no release has it.

--- a/src/wayland/seat/pointer.rs
+++ b/src/wayland/seat/pointer.rs
@@ -250,7 +250,9 @@

             with_pointer_constraint(self, &pointer, |constraint| {
                 if let Some(constraint) = constraint {
-                    constraint.deactivate();
+                    if constraint.is_active() {
+                        constraint.deactivate();
+                    }
                 }
             });
         }
